{
  "id": "Lyo.Outbox",
  "name": "Lyo.Outbox",
  "area": "Core",
  "tagline": "Outbox contract. Enqueue records a message on the caller's transaction. Publishing is a separate dispatcher.",
  "description": "IOutbox does not reference a broker. Delivery is at-least-once. Consumers dedupe on the row id. Enqueue does not commit and does not accept a caller-supplied hash.",
  "features": [
    "**Enqueue first.** Write the outbox row, and write business rows only when Inserted is true. A duplicate leaves the caller transaction open. A different payload rolls it back."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Enqueue, then business rows",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "await using var tx = await db.Database.BeginTransactionAsync(ct);\nvar enqueued = await outbox.EnqueueAsync(tx.GetDbTransaction(), message, ct);\nif (!enqueued.Inserted) {\n    await tx.RollbackAsync(ct);\n    return enqueued;\n}\nawait tx.CommitAsync(ct);"
    }
  ],
